The partner-book reader's m3-v1 profile and its parsers, ported for the
tape-intake environment's date tool and the desk's reading of a delivery.

Source       packages/partner-book/src/m3-v1.ts, and excelSerialToIsoDate from
             packages/partner-book/src/vendored/xlsx.ts (vendored from the
             servicing app's repository; packages/partner-book/src/vendored/VENDORED_FROM)
Ported       2026-10-23; m3-v1.ts copied again 2026-10-26, when the reader
             learned to read a loan number as a workbook's writer stores it

m3-v1.ts here is that file byte for byte except one import: the profile takes
excelSerialToIsoDate from the vendored workbook reader, which imports
node:zlib, and an environment runs in the browser playground, whose bundle
stops on any node: module but three. So the import names ./xlsx-serial.js,
which holds the reader's "Excel serial dates" section (MS_PER_DAY and the
function) copied character for character under a comment that says so. The
kernel imports are the same in both packages. Nothing else may be edited:
src/__tests__/tape-intake.test.ts compares m3-v1.ts with its source but for
that import, and the section with the vendored file's, and fails on any
difference. Lint and Prettier skip this directory for the reason they skip
the vendored trees.

What each is for. `parseDateIso` is the parse_date tool: what the reader
reads a date cell as, on a given day. `profileHeadersPresent` and
`mapTapeRow` are the desk's reading of a delivery (desk.ts): the required
headers it refuses a file for, and each row's exceptions, as parseBook in
packages/partner-book/src/book.ts gathers them. A test reads every task's
delivery with readBook itself and holds the desk's reading to it. A delivery
is CSV, so the desk leaves mapTapeRow's file kind at its default, a CSV's,
which is how readBook reads that file too.

Not ported: book.ts (its node:crypto hash and @hm/shared/portfolio's schema,
which imports node:crypto too) and tabular.ts. The delivery is CSV the life
generator wrote, which the tape-intake tools split themselves.

To take a change from the reader, copy m3-v1.ts again and rewrite the same
import.
